comments.body:
@lisad There are no longer specific requirements on what the communication looks like.  I got rid of all of that "MUST produce the largest index successfully evaluated" language, because there's no longer any need for it.  We just care about the outcome.

So I don't think the table makes sense anymore.  If we want to rework this as an "Implementing applicator communication" appendix we can (that would probably be helpful), but I think it would look rather different.

I just couldn't figure out how to keep this as it focuses on the exact annotation values, which are no longer required at all.

@awwright 

> it would suffice to say that JSON Schema is only defined in terms of an input, not as a mutation on the input,

What is the practical implication of this on interoperability for something like filling in default values, or like the `transform` extension keyword I used in an example for the mailing list?
